 #:seon.task{:name "agent-form-writes-name-an-unwritten-evaluation"
             :kind :function
             :intent "On live e405f51be (one-commit A) every write an agent form makes on its branch refuses 'Nothing found for entity id [`:seon.cluster.eval/id` <this form>]': the evaluation's receipt lookup ref (`seon.sci.eval/evaluate`, receipt at eval.clj:4341-4343) names the evaluation entity that is written only at settlement. It breaks (`seon.db/transact!` ...) at the REPL and every test run from the agent REPL (`my.test/run-owned` admission), so no agent can prove a change. Reproduced 2026-09-26 20:38Z and 20:46Z on branch merge-cut1-opus (evals 78f381684a44, 82cf53bace3b). Still live on 7c56fb226 default (2026-10-08, lane fs-root): (`seon.config/apply!` {`:seon.boot/cluster-name` \"default\" `:seon.config/manifest` {`:seon.config.fs/working-root` \"/Users/sean/src/seon\"}}) from agent fs-root's SCI context refused the same way in 385 ms and 38,412 armed calls; the same apply in JVM mode with the branch connection passed explicitly committed in 244 ms."
             :must-read #{seon.sci.eval/evaluate}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/merge-cut1-opus-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "program-change-check-scans-the-whole-history"
             :kind :function
             :intent "installation-covers-program-change? (install-evaluated-rows!, every defining batch) no longer scans the history: its cost follows the settlement's datoms. The remaining cost was measured in a throwaway root (2026-10-08, HEAD ff351d2b5) at 15-138 ms of a 19-143 ms install-evaluated-rows! in a defn pass (MCP 138 ms first, 15 ms second; model 38 and 17 ms), and it was NOT the pulls of non-program entities (1-2 ms): it was the component-parent join, a query over (`seon.db/history` after) at 6-12 ms per settlement against 0.6 ms on the final value. Fixed: the join reads the final value (a parent that lost a child is itself among the datoms) and only program rows are pulled in full (ledger PB-02, option 2). After the change the check measures 6-38 ms (MCP) and 9-17 ms (model). What remains of install-evaluated-rows! (about 25 ms in a model pass, 5 ms in an MCP pass) is install-row! and the snapshot update."
             :must-read #{seon.sci.eval/install-evaluated-rows!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/perf-admit-tests-opus-2026-09-26.md" "docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/model-pass/pb-02-notes.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "program-movement-is-checked-three-ways-per-form"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Each form asks whether its program moved three ways: trusted-evaluation over the loaded-identity atom, acquired-database? with loaded-program-current? over the program-identity cache (and reacquires inside evaluate), and installation-covers-program-change? after settlement. The JVM loaded-identity check is the ruled one; the branch-program check belongs once to the turn fork, never inside evaluate. Measured 2026-10-08 (HEAD ff351d2b5): in the model pass after a contracted defn acquired-database? costs 14-31 ms (about 1-2 ms otherwise), all of it acquisition-attributes (2 calls, 42 ms in the first run) re-deriving program-attributes and projection-attributes for the new projection, which program-attributes documents as about 50 ms per projection over the packaged population; the identity and basis comparisons are 0 ms. Removing it needs the derivation keyed by the schema content that changed rather than by projection."
             :must-read #{seon.sci.eval/trusted-evaluation seon.sci.eval/acquired-database? seon.sci.eval/installation-covers-program-change? seon.sci.eval/evaluate}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/eval-path-audit-2026-09-26.md"}}
