r-ctx` of root's live context, whose contract loop re-arms each contracted interpreted function with `sci.core/bind-root!`, copying the callee's Var into the fork while the inherited test keeps calling root's Var; `seon.sci.eval/acquired-database?` answers equal, so nothing repairs it, and the step's world forked that base. Interim: `seon.test/clean-request-handle` builds the world with `seon.sci.eval/base-ctx` from the branch's definitions; the agent's own base stays stale until SCI Var handles are context-owned (docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/sci-fork-vars/sci-sol.md). The check fixture (`seon.test-support/with-running-agent`) does not reproduce the stale base. Done when a test the branch inherits calls the branch's current Var of its callee."
